# Verified together with the primary hunk: both `git apply --check -p1` clean, zero offset,
# on the same freshly-scp'd pre-image pair; both applied; both compiled by the engine
# interpreter.
#
# ---- THE THIRD FILE: the load side, which is what makes the other two live ----------
# Written as a COMMENTED block with lowercase key names, for the day the tool can carry
# it. They are comments on purpose: this file is shell-sourced, and a second live
# `tree_v2_5_1_target_abs=` would win over the primary entry's and silently re-point a
# verdict at the wrong file. The names are lowercase because `TREE_FIELDS`
# (kvtier-patch.sh:328) and `tree_field()` (:354) only ever read lowercase suffixes.
#   module                  vllm.v1.worker.gpu.kv_connector
#   klass                   ActiveKVConnector
#   git_rel                 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/kv_connector.py
